    "q-216734": {
      "dom_id": "step-q216734",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$(7{u}^{2}-6v)(v-u)=${{field-1}}${u}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${u}^{2}v\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$uv\\,-$\n{{field-4}}${v}^{2}$",
      "worked_solution": "We take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(7{u}^{2}-6v)(v-u) & = \\\\ 7{u}^{2}(v-u)+(-6v)(v-u) & = \\\\ 7{u}^{2}v-7{u}^{3}-6{v}^{2}+6uv & = \\\\ -7{u}^{3}+7{u}^{2}v+6uv-6{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot simplify the above expression any further because there are no like terms.",
