      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$(2{c}^{4}+3d)({c}^{4}+2d)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{c}^{4}+3d)({c}^{4}+2d) & = \\\\ 2{c}^{4}({c}^{4}+2d)+3d({c}^{4}+2d) & = \\\\ 2{c}^{8}+4{c}^{4}d+3{c}^{4}d+6{d}^{2} & = \\\\ 2{c}^{8}+7{c}^{4}d+6{d}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
